    ),
  )

  A traditional lab sells products and services. An aligned network helps practices build long-term competitive strength.

  That difference matters.

  When the lab is only a vendor, the relationship is transactional. When the lab is part of a larger aligned network, the relationship can become strategic.

  ALN was designed to move beyond the transactional lab model. The goal is not simply to process orders. The goal is to help independent practices maintain choice, improve performance, strengthen relationships, and participate in the long-term value of the network they support.

